WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.639 --> 00:00:08.700
Marauding space aliens and their ilk aren't
the true dangers that lurk within your favorite

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:13.309
video games. What you really need to be worried
about are blood clots, a lack of movement,

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:17.850
and a vulnerability to game-induced psychosis.
It might look like you’re just sitting there

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:22.490
on your couch, but the reality of what your
body and mind are going through is pretty

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:27.050
intense. There have been many unfortunate
gamers who've paid for their passion. Here

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:31.730
are a few heartbreaking stories to remind
us that video games can be pretty serious

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:33.600
business.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.370
The Berzerk heart attack

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:41.000
It may not look like much, but Berzerk is
one of the earliest known examples of a video

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.140
game ending in actual tragedy. In April of 1982,
an 18-year-old named Peter Bukowski landed

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:52.699
a couple of high scores on a Berzerk arcade
cabinet before collapsing from a heart attack.

00:00:52.699 --> 00:00:57.690
Doctors later found out that he had a compromised
cardiovascular system, which was agitated

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:03.809
beyond repair by the game. An October 1982
article in Video Games Magazine cites studies

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:09.640
that used Pong to measure physiological reactions
to video game induced stress, dating as far

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:17.380
as 1977. The body’s physical reaction to
on-screen events was found to be pretty significant.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.590
The EverQuest tragedy

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:25.659
EverQuest, affectionately called "EverCrack"
or "NeverRest" by its many dedicated fans,

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:32.149
is an online game known for drawing in easily-addicted
gamers. The draw is so intense that it’s

00:01:32.149 --> 00:01:37.420
well known to break apart relationships and
cause people to ignore real-life responsibilities.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:43.090
Shawn Woolley took his EverQuest passion to
the extreme in 2002, quitting his job to play

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:48.289
full-time. After he ignored a Thanksgiving
invitation from his family, his loved ones

00:01:48.289 --> 00:01:53.509
found Woolley lifeless  in front of his computer
from a self-inflicted gunshot wound—with

00:01:53.509 --> 00:01:58.600
EverQuest still running. Woolley took his
own life for unknown reasons, but evidence

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:03.409
suggested that it may have been related to
a troubled in-game relationship. Shawn’s

00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:06.990
mother later accused the publisher of intentionally
harming her son:

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:11.230
"I didn't know the game was written to get
him in there, to draw him in there and to

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:14.370
keep him in there so that they could make
money."

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.260
The Legend of Mir 3 stabbing

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:22.580
It’s another online gaming incident with
tragic, real-life ramifications. Legend of

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:28.590
Mir players Qiu Chengwei and Zhu Caoyuan jointly
earned a very rare, very virtual Dragon Sabre

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:34.980
sword in 2005. But Zhu decided to sell the
sword on eBay without Qiu's consent, earning

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:40.760
around $870 for the sale. The two players
couldn't come to a reasonable agreement as

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:46.170
to proper disbursal of payment for the sword,
so Qiu stabbed Zhu in his sleep.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:52.239
Qiu was sentenced to life in prison, but will
be eligible for parole in 2020.

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:53.230
The FarmVille maniac

00:02:53.230 --> 00:03:00.400
Sadly, even FarmVille can turn evil in the
wrong hands. Alexandra Tobias, a 22-year-old

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:05.260
mother, was so addicted to the game that she
shook her three-month-old son to lifelessness because

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:10.099
his crying interrupted her playing. Tobias
received a 50-year prison sentence for her

00:03:10.099 --> 00:03:15.650
actions in 2011. At one point, she allegedly
confessed to a fellow inmate that she hit

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:20.659
her baby's head against the computer monitor
in the process of trying to shake him into

00:03:20.659 --> 00:03:21.209
silence.

00:03:21.209 --> 00:03:27.040
Unfortunately, it’s not all that uncommon
for children to suffer while parents game.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.620
The World of Warcraft maniac

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:34.300
The story of Rebecca Colleen Christie offers
a worst-case scenario when it comes to game

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:39.380
addiction. Christie spent such an inordinate
amount of time playing Warcraft that she allowed

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:44.870
her three-year-old daughter to starve.
Prosecutors found that Christie had just engaged

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:51.110
in a nonstop 15-hour Warcraft session prior
to finally calling 911 for her daughter, who

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:56.269
was found unresponsive. She was subsequently
sentenced to 25 years in prison for the crime

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.569
of neglect.

00:03:57.569 --> 00:04:03.110
On the other hand, some parents go above and
beyond for their kids, as we see next.

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:06.420
Water intoxication for a Nintendo Wii

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:11.409
In 2007, the Nintendo Wii was still hard to
get in the US, so the Sacramento-based radio

00:04:11.409 --> 00:04:17.610
station KDND decided to run a contest giving
one of the consoles away. The challenge? Drink

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:23.330
a huge amount of water without urinating,
and whoever went last won the Nintendo system.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:28.320
Unfortunately, water intoxication can be fatal,
and contestant Jennifer Strange collapsed

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:33.940
and perished after failing to win the prize for
her children. The station fired ten employees

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:38.780
and lost a $16 million lawsuit for the juvenile
stunt.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:41.220
The Ingress incident

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:45.860
A mobile app that requires you to get up and
move around seems like a great idea, until

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:51.520
that app sends you directly into traffic.
Gabriel Leao was an unfortunate casualty of

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:57.860
truly mobile gaming. While playing Ingress
in 2014, the 16-year-old Brazilian teen lost

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:02.220
track of his surroundings while rushing to
a "portal" in the game, and was hit by

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:07.700
an oncoming bus. While Ingress has built-in
limits to prevent certain unsafe behaviors,

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:12.120
there was nothing to stop an absorbed and
enthusiastic kid from walking into a busy

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:17.380
street. The limits also didn't help Frank
Maxwell, a 48-year-old father who drowned

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:22.230
near a pier in Ireland while playing the game
in 2015.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.140
The Slender stabbing… and arson

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:29.860
Slender: The Arrival didn't directly slay
anyone, but an obsession with its main baddie

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:36.050
influenced a few impressionable young girls
to do some insidious things. In May of 2014,

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:41.840
two 12-year-old girls from Cincinnati, Ohio
stabbed their classmate 19 times, believing

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:47.050
that they had to axe someone in order to
appease the mythical villain, Slender Man.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:52.310
Just as disturbing is the case of a 14-year-old
girl who set her family's Florida home on

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:57.310
fire, with her mother and younger brother
still inside. Fortunately, no one was harmed.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:06:02.190
The girl was also obsessed with Slender Man
lore, and reportedly started the fire in order

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:04.650
to gain his favor.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:09.150
The deadly Diablo III, Halo, StarCraft, and
Warcraft marathons

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:14.270
Gamers, please note: you have to get up and
move around sometimes, because the list of

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:20.160
losses from sitting on your butt and twiddling
your thumbs just keeps growing. In 2012, an

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:25.160
18-year-old named Chuang passed away in an Internet
cafe in Taiwan after 40 continuous hours of

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:31.850
Diablo III—the second marathon game-related
tragedy in Taiwan that year. In 2011, England’s

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:38.620
Chris Staniforth passed away from deep vein thrombosis
after playing 12 hours of Halo. In 2005, Lee

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:44.450
Seung Seop passed away in South Korea after 50 hours
of StarCraft. The list doesn’t end there,

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:46.820
and it goes on quite a while.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:51.530
Moral of the story: don't take extended gameplay
lightly. Even when you're in the thick of

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:57.160
the action, remember that the pause button
exists. Take a break, stand up, get some water,

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:01.220
and move around every once in a while. It’ll
be there when you get back.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:05.090
Thanks for watching. Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:05.720
you just saw.

